                <pb facs="0673" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg557"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/4430: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-30T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>240. Your telegram 376 of November 27, noon. Can you inform the Department what
                    action foreign powers chiefly interested contemplate in case customs are
                    seized?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
